 * 3. Attempt to update a setting using an obviously malformed settingId (not a UUID).
 *    - Expect a validation error (typically 400) response and ensure no resource is changed.
 * 4. Optionally, test that a successful update with a real settingId (when properly used) does not throw error,
 *    but this is excluded from this test as the intent is to cover invalid ID cases.
 */
