 * 4. Attempt to update the just-created moderation action as this non-admin user, expecting an access denied error (authorization failure).
 * 5. Assert that an error is thrown and no update is performed.
 *
 * Note: This test assumes the SDK/API context only grants write access for moderation actions to authorized actors. If privilege simulation is not possible without a full auth system, mock/prune connection headers or emulate context at least to the degree that the endpoint will reject a clearly unauthorized request. The test focuses on backend access control, not data shape validation.
 */
export async function test_api_discussionBoard_test_admin_update_moderation_action_with_insufficient_permission(
  connection: api.IConnection,
) {
